        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-29 22:09:22.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_51b",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_51b\n\ntest_51b counts the directories it really created with\n\"find $dir -maxdepth 1 | wc -l\". find stats every one of the\n65k entries, and that count sat between the parallel create\nand the parallel unlink as a pause of 90 to 100 seconds on a\nVM, while nothing else ran. The count before the parallel\nchange was \"ls -U\", which only reads the directory.\n\nUse \"ls -U\" again. Nothing it checks changes: the count still\nvalidates the creates, and the second ls -U after the first\nunlink is unchanged. The count is now exact (65636) rather\nthan one high from find listing $dir itself, and the\nper-process unlink count stays 32768.\n\nOn a rocky9 VM with ldiskfs, three runs of ONLY=51b each:\nbefore 160s, 128s, 121s; after 46s, 48s, 50s.\n\nCI runs this test 14991 times per 30 days at a mean of 180s;\nsaving about 88s per run is roughly 1.32M s, or 366 hours,\nper 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=51b\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ifb9d082e378204c8fb8fdaae922818d1034e0227\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
